 75NI c  2010Ho12: {+9}Be({+86}Kr,X) E=140 MeV/nucleon; fully-ionized {+86}Kr   
 75NI2c  beam, A1900 fragment separator at NSCL facility using B|r-|DE-B|r      
 75NI3c  method. After separation, the mixed beam was implanted into the        
 75NI4c  NSCL |b-counting system (BCS) consisting of stacks of Si PIN           
 75NI5c  detectors, a double-sided Si strip detector (DSSD) for implantation of 
 75NI6c  ions, and six single-sided Si strip detectors (SSSD) followed by two   
 75NI7c  Si PIN diodes. The identification of each implanted event was made     
 75NI8c  from energy loss, time-of-flight information and magnetic rigidity.    
 75NI9c  The implantation detector measured time and position of ion            
 75NIAc  implantations and |b decays. Neutrons were detected with NERO detector.
 75NIBc  Measured |b- and |bn-correlated events with ion implants;              
 75NICc  half-life of {+75}Ni and delayed-neutron emission probability.         
